  {
   "id": 674149,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Consider new product adopter categories and answer the following questions.\n<ol style=\"list-style-type: lower-alpha;margin-left:1em;padding-left:1em;\">\n<li>Do you believe that consumers are always in the same category? For example, once a laggard, always a laggard? Can someone be a laggard in one category and an early majority in another?</li>\n<li>What impact do these categories have on new product development?</li>\n<li>Can you think of a time or product category where marketing would want to push more consumers into one category?</li>\n</ol>",
